{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> passes through the center of, and is tangent to, circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. The area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square inches. \nThen the area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, in square inches, is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d24eeeebf70932dc45bd3b04acaee4a1a2719f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }8\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }8\\sqrt{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }8\\sqrt{\\pi}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }16\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }16\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"446\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03da0997cf51055b17f56ff32b23c9911b04889e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),50)); draw(circle((-25,0),25)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and touches the center of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the diameter of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>That means circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is twice as big as circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is four times as big as circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> square inches, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and touches the center of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, the diameter of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Applying the area formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a29e7889fad76777233bc77041cf045d9fb6f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\pi r^2$\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to solve for the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24c39ea60706cb36098ea6a6287e09e34974fd46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 = \\pi r^2\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/96869f2b40d9646590b1ffec7155d897962967e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4}{\\pi} = r^2\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907e64d3ff77a3f71367576931df2d01ae8d203f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>That means the diameter of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (or the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/78606923008350c5781aad40b223f93a46f454e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"28\" height=\"41\" />.  Apply the area formula again to find the area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0a3a434db3ce72f119c76f1940a955fce1ad44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\pi (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}})^2 = \\pi \\cdot \\frac{4}{\\pi} = 16\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Proble